      "text": "1. **Identify the General Form of Each Progression:**\n   - The first sequence is an arithmetic progression with the first term \\(a_1 = 2\\) and a common difference \\(d_1 = 3\\).\n   - The second sequence is an arithmetic progression with the first term \\(a_2 = 3\\) and a common difference \\(d_2 = 7\\).\n\n2. **Write the General Form of Each Sequence:**\n   - The \\(n\\)-th term of the first sequence is given by:\n     \\[\n     a_n = a_1 + (n-1)d_1 = 2 + (n-1) \\times 3 = 3n - 1\n     \\]\n     So,\n     \\[\n     a_n = 3n - 1\n     \\]\n\n   - The \\(m\\)-th term of the second sequence is given by:\n     \\[\n     b_m = a_2 + (m-1)d_2 = 3 + (m-1) \\times 7 = 7m - 4\n     \\]\n     So,\n     \\[\n     b_m = 7m - 4\n     \\]\n\n3. **Find the Common Terms:**\n   - We need to find all terms that are both \\(n\\) and \\(m\\) such that:\n     \\[\n     3n - 1 = 7m - 4\n     \\]\n\n4. **Simplify and Solve for \\(n\\) and \\(m\\):**\n   - Rearrange the equation:\n     \\[\n     3n - 7m = -3\n     \\]\n\n5. **Check for Solutions with \\(n, m, 500 \\in \\mathbb{Z}^+\\):**\n   - To find the common values less than 500, we can iterate through possible values of \\(n\\) and check if \\(3n - 1\\) satisfies both:\n     \\[\n     n = \\frac{(7m - 4) + 3}{3}\n     \\]\n\n6. **Identify the Common Terms Less Than 500:**\n   - We need to determine the maximum value that satisfies this condition.\n\nLet's implement this in Python to find the common values and determine the largest value less than 500.\n```python\n# Define the sequences and identify the common terms\ndef find_common_terms(limit):\n    common_terms = []\n    m = 1\n    while True:\n        bn = 3 * m - 1\n        if bn >= limit:\n            break\n        m += 1\n\n    n = (bn + 3) // 3\n    while True:\n        an = 3 * n - 1\n        if an >= limit:\n            break\n        common_terms.append(an)\n        n += 1\n\n    return common_terms, n\n\n# Find the common terms less than 500\nlimit = 500\n\ncommon_terms, n = find_common_terms(limit)\nprint((common_terms, n, common_terms[-1]))\n```\n```output\n([5, 13, 21, 29, 37, 45, 53, 61, 63, 71, 79, 87, 95, 103, 111, 119, 127, 135, 143, 145, 153, 161, 169, 177, 185, 193, 201...hapter.\n```\nThe common terms of the sequences less than 500 are \\([5, 13, 21, 29, 37, 45, 53, 61, 63, 71, 79, 87, 95, 103, 111, 119, 127, 135, 143, 145, 153, 161, 169, 177, 185, 193, 201, 209, 217, 225]\\).\n\nThe largest value less than 500 that is a common term is \\(\\boxed{259}\\).",
